<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tinganes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tinganes is a small rocky peninsula in the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torshavn">Tórshavn</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faroe-islands">Faroe Islands</a>. From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> it was the meeting place of the Alting, the islands' assembly, and it is regarded as one of the oldest parliamentary meeting places in the world. Its cluster of old turf-roofed wooden buildings now houses the offices of the Faroese government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tinganes.jpg" alt="Tinganes" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stig Nygaard from Copenhagen, Denmark · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tinganes_57.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
